From 50daeaff7293a8624b2d8ba63e86be2fd7a5d8f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:26:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ability_runtime: always re-arm the uv timer task when none is
 queued

OHOSLoopHandler::OnTriggered drives the libuv loop of the JS main thread
from the event runner: it runs uv_run(UV_RUN_NOWAIT), then posts
"uv_timer_task" for uv_backend_timeout() and records the deadline in
lastTimeStamp_. It returns early, without posting, when the new deadline
equals lastTimeStamp_, so that an identical task is not posted twice.

That is only correct while the previous task is still queued. When
OnTriggered runs from the timer task itself (haveTimerTask_ was just
cleared) and uv_run did not expire the timer, the deadline is unchanged,
OnTriggered returns, and no timer task is left at all. From then on no
libuv timer of the loop fires again: setTimeout/setInterval in the app
stop for good, while UI events and every other task keep running.
Nothing re-arms it, because pending timers never make the epoll fd
readable.

uv_run expires nothing when uv_now() is still a millisecond short of the
timer: libuv reads CLOCK_MONOTONIC_COARSE when its resolution is 1 ms
(CONFIG_HZ=1000), which can lag the CLOCK_MONOTONIC wake-up of the event
runner by a tick. The same happens when uv__run_timers is interrupted
(SUPPORT_INTERRUPT). Upstream only avoids it on device_company
"emulator" builds (RUNTIME_EMULATOR); the Oniro emulator is HZ=1000 and
not such a build, and the race hits it within seconds on WHPX and on
contended KVM hosts.

Skip the re-post only when a timer task is still queued.

Reproduced on emulator_x86_64 (7.0.0.39, KVM, host cores contended) with
a 1000 ms + 24 ms setInterval probe: stock libruntime stopped 3 of 3
runs, two before the first tick; with this change 3 of 3 kept ticking.

Change-Id: Ia44a5e899ffc4fe4ab82e37d58151275b2c349aa
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
---
 frameworks/native/runtime/ohos_loop_handler.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/frameworks/native/runtime/ohos_loop_handler.cpp b/frameworks/native/runtime/ohos_loop_handler.cpp
index 46027671c0..ab954ab0d4 100644
--- a/frameworks/native/runtime/ohos_loop_handler.cpp
+++ b/frameworks/native/runtime/ohos_loop_handler.cpp
@@ -50,9 +50,16 @@ void OHOSLoopHandler::OnTriggered()
     }
 
     int64_t timeStamp = static_cast<int64_t>(uv_now(uvLoop_)) + timeout;
+    // Skipping the re-post is only safe while the task for this deadline is
+    // still queued. When OnTriggered runs from that task (haveTimerTask_ was
+    // just cleared) and uv_run did not expire the timer -- uv_now() is read
+    // from CLOCK_MONOTONIC_COARSE, which can lag the event runner's clock by
+    // a tick, or uv__run_timers was interrupted -- the deadline is unchanged
+    // and returning here leaves no timer task at all: every libuv timer of
+    // the loop (setTimeout/setInterval) stops for good.
     // we don't check timestamp in emulator for computer clock is inaccurate
 #ifndef RUNTIME_EMULATOR
-    if (timeStamp == lastTimeStamp_) {
+    if (haveTimerTask_ && timeStamp == lastTimeStamp_) {
         return;
     }
 #endif
-- 
